#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:1
msgid "Changing the Working Directory in a Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:3
msgid ""
"Each recipe line is executed by a new shell, so if you change the working "
"directory on one line, it won’t have an effect on later lines:"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:13
msgid ""
"There are a couple ways around this. One is to call `cd` on the same line as "
"the command you want to run:"
msgstr ""

#: src/changing-the-working-directory-in-a-recipe.md:21
msgid ""
"The other is to use a shebang recipe. Shebang recipe bodies are extracted "
"and run as scripts, so a single shell instance will run the whole thing, and "
"thus a `cd` on one line will affect later lines, just like a shell script:"
msgstr ""
